[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     804[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // Row 25 — unchecked cache indices (see also level3_gjk.rs)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     805[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // ===========================================================================
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     806[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     807[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// Row 25 — `cache->count` is never checked against `iA[3]`/`iB[3]`, and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     808[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// indices are never checked against the proxy's vertex count. Indices inside
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     809[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// the initialised vertex range must agree bit-for-bit; `count > 3` reads the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     810[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// adjacent `iB`/`div` bytes of the SAME struct, which is defined-enough that
